The formula Shade is a state-level formula, but it was used as a PROPERTY (or PROPERTIES), where a temporal formula is typically expected. State-level formulas used as PROPERTY or PROPERTIES are only checked in the initial state. To verify that the formula Shade holds in all states of every behavior, use INVARIANT Shade instead. Alternatively, applying the "always" temporal operator ([]) to the state-level formula Shade changes it into a temporal formula, asserting that Shade holds in all states of every behavior. See https://explain.tlapl.us/invariants-and-properties for additional details.
